Description:
Drawing; from a collection of sixty-one: "Tibetan Nobleman in government service in Official Attire and Hair-do". Adult male in decorated costume wearing a long ear-ring and ornament in his hair.
The Tibetan nobleman "Porong Se Kunsang Shamba" twenty-six years old, was interpreter at the Red Cross in Patan, Nepal. He had learned English at the mission school in Kalimpong, India. The artist gave him English conversation lessons and Shamba told her about the traditions of the Tibetan aristocracy. His hair-do, attire and single ear-ring were typical of a Tibetan aristocrat. Petan, Nepal, April 24th, 1961. 
Chalk and crayon.;

Drawing; from a collection of sixty-one: "Tsipr"; a young Tibetan woman with child on her lap, she is holding a string of beads in her hand. Bodhnath, Nepal, February 1962.
Tsipr's husband was quite well to do and had given Tsipr necklaces and beautiful ornaments. The artist made several drawings of her as well as an oil painting.
Chalk and crayon.;

